What is Routing in Express js ?
=============================
→ Routing in Express.js means deciding which code should run for a specific URL and HTTP method.
→ Routing tells Express what to do when a user hits a particular API or page.
→ If we have routes like /orders or /products, routing maps these URLs to the correct controller functions.

🔹 Using Router (industry style)
const router = require("express").Router();
router.post("/order", createOrder);
router.get("/order/:id", getOrder);
module.exports = router;
